:: Millers Babysitting Isaiah Desk [nobr]

/* Intro */
As you stand in <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>’s room, sitting at his desk, your curiosity gets the better of you as you begin to snoop around. You’re not really looking for anything in particular but just looking to see what you can find. <span style="Color: LightGreen">Maybe a naughty stash of images, maybe some neat drawings, maybe something embarrassing that you can tease <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> about sometime. The boy is so cool it would be fun to see his more childish and human side. So, you begin to peek around.</span> <br>
<br>

<<set _random to random(1, 4)>>
<<if _random == 1>>
    Then you spot a notebook sticking out from under his desk. You pick it up and begin to flip through the pages, finding them filled with handwritten lyrics and doodles. The words are raw, passionate, and surprisingly deep for his young age. Some lines are scratched out while others are underlined or circled. One page even has a few musical notes sketched alongside some lyrics. <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    It is pretty impressive and you read some of the lines in your head, though can’t think of what the melody or rhythm would be with just the drawings of the notes alone. Maybe someday <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> will play some of his own songs for you, if he isn’t too embarrassed. You carefully place the notebook back where you found it, making a mental note not to mention it to anyone. It feels a bit too personal to share. <br>
    <<needChange "Fun" 3>>
    <br>
    [[Continue|OC Miller House Isaiah Room]]

<<elseif _random == 2>>
    You notice one of the drawers on the desk is slightly ajar. Unable to resist, you pull it open to find an assortment of random items shoved inside. Earbuds, a half-finished puzzle cube, a mini basketball, and a few crumpled pieces of paper. As you sift through, you find a photo of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> and his dad backstage at what looks like a concert. They’re both smiling and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> is holding a microphone. <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="Color: LightGreen">The picture is very cute, showing just how much care these two have for each other. You can’t help but smile as you quickly and carefully tuck the picture back in. You feel a little guilty for snooping, though are happy you got to see such a happy photo.</span> <br>
    <<needChange "Fun" 3>>
    <br>
    [[Continue|OC Miller House Isaiah Room]]

<<elseif _random == 3>>
    As you sit, you notice a small tin box pushed into the corner. You reach for it and pop it open, revealing an assortment of trinkets: a keychain, a ticket stub from a concert, and a small, folded note. You unfold the paper and see a messy scrawl that reads: <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Never stop being you, my little rockstar -Dad.”</span> <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="Color: LightGreen">Your chest tightens as you read it, the simple words very clearly being very important to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>. This little note must have been saved since it meant so much to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>. You carefully fold the note back, handling it with extreme care, as you put it back in the box and close the lid. While the note wasn’t anything embarrassing or naughty, it felt extremely personal and you decide you’ve snooped enough for the time being.</span> <br>
    <<needChange "Fun" 3>>
    <br>
    [[Continue|OC Miller House Isaiah Room]]

<<elseif _random == 4>>
    As you are rummaging through <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>’s desk drawer, your fingers graze against something crumpled and tucked away in the back. Curious, you pull it out – a wrinkled piece of paper folded so tightly, that it’s clear <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> doesn’t want it to be found. You hesitate for a moment, but unfold it carefully, revealing a sharp, deliberate handwriting. <br>
    <br>
    Your eyes widen as you begin to read, realizing the letter is from someone named <span style="Color: DarkTurquoise">Niki</span>. <span style="Color: LightCoral">The words hit like a punch to the gut as you realized this is <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>’s mother being very vicious: <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>, I don’t know why you keep trying to act like you matter. You’re a disappointment and you always will be.”</span> Your chest tightens as you read further, the cruel works spiraling into something even darker, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You’re nothing but a burden. I wish you and those gremlins hadn’t ever been born. I only had ya’ll because your pathetic father wanted kids. My life is much better without y’all, so never contact me or mention my name publicly. And if this letter gets out, I’ll make sure you regret it.”</span> <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Eyes: "Sad",
                    Blush: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="Color: LightCoral">You feel a deep, gnawing sadness from him, paired with a surge of anger at how anyone could do something so cruel to their own child. You lean back at the chair, staring at the drawer and the paper in your hand, torn between the guilt of snooping and the overwhelming urge to support <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> in any way you can.</span> <br>
    <br>
    [[Continue|OC Miller House Isaiah Room]]
<</if>>